{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01HQTv1S6PWcfuMsAFFZPRQF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The root issue is `NoClassDefFoundError: Could not initialize class org.springframework.cglib.proxy.Enhancer`. This is a Spring CGLIB issue.\n\n`org.springframework.cglib.proxy.Enhancer` is Spring's repackaged CGLIB. This is bundled inside `spring-core`. The issue is that CGLIB Enhancer initialization is failing.\n\nIn Java 17+, CGLIB has issues with module system (module access restrictions). This project is Java 1.8 as per the conventions, but the JVM running this may be a newer version.\n\nLet me check what JVM version is actually running and what Spring version is being used.\n\n\nThe \"Could not initialize class Enhancer\" error typically means ASM, the bytecode generation library, is struggling to generate code for the target JVM. If Spring Framework 4.3.4 is being used with an older ASM version on Java 17+, there's likely a class file format incompatibility where the old ASM doesn't understand Java 9+ bytecode structures. I need to verify the actual Java version being used.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":782,"cache_read_input_tokens":60287,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":782},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6547310c-c57f-4bb9-bd57-530175104ef3","uuid":"ddc0d61b-510f-4e62-8210-fd4b166021db"}
