{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01BtZ8A2ttBFHsU9H437hLSV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The pom.xml compiles with `source=1.8` and `target=1.8`, which means the compiled class files will have Java 8 format (class version 52). This should be fine for Spring 4.3.4's bundled CGLIB/ASM to read.\n\nBut wait - the maven compiler plugin version 3.11.0 with source/target 1.8 on Java 25... In Java 21+, `--source 1.8` might not be supported anymore! Java removed support for very old source/target levels. Actually in Java 17+, there are warnings, but in Java 22+ there might be restrictions.\n\n\nThe compilation actually succeeds, so the class files are being generated in Java 8 format - the real problem is happening at runtime when CGLIB tries to process those class files.\n\nSpring 4.3.4 bundles its own CGLIB with ASM 5.x, which should handle Java 8 class files just fine. But the `NoClassDefFoundError` for the Enhancer class suggests it failed during static initialization, and now every attempt to use it fails. The root cause was an earlier exception during that initialization phase.\n\nLooking at the LoadingCache code, when createEntry tries to load a cache item, it wraps the loader in a FutureTask and then calls get() on it. If that execution fails, it throws an \"Unable to load cache item\" error, which means something went wrong during the actual loading process.\n\nI need to dig into the full stack trace to see what exception the loader itself is throwing underneath that ExecutionException wrapper.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5163,"cache_read_input_tokens":61700,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5163},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6547310c-c57f-4bb9-bd57-530175104ef3","uuid":"9e80f9f8-52ec-4fe7-bf34-fb275c28411a"}
